</mj-text>
    <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif;" color="#000000">
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 400; margin-top: 2px !important;">
    Trump fires Noem
  </h2>
</mj-text>
<mj-image
  border-radius="10px"
  padding="10px 12px"
  width="600px"
  src="https://www.presidentialsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
  alt="Trump fires Noem"
  href="https://www.presidentialsummary.com/"
/>
<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>What happened? </strong>President Trump <a href="https://edition.cnn.com/2026/03/05/politics/kristi-noem-trump-homeland-security-replace" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none;
                border-bottom: 2px solid #4d3060;
                color: black;">fired Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem</a> and would nominate Oklahoma Republican Sen. Markwayne Mullin in her place. The decision was announced a few days after Noem faced a grilling on Capitol Hill by GOP members and Democrats. Trump said she would be moving to serve as the Special Envoy for the Shield of the Americas. Noem is the first Cabinet secretary to exit during Trump’s second term.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>Criticism:</strong> Noem received bipartisan criticism for the agency’s handling of the immigration crackdown and delays in emergency response. She oversaw a team of agents who shot dead two US citizens and called them both domestic terrorists in the immediate aftermath. Additonally she spent taxpayer currency on department ads featuring herself, and faced unrelenting rumours of an affair with her top adviser, Corey Lewandowski. Noem denied the affair.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>Who is Markwayne Mullin?</strong>  He is a <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c4g5xd2p7vqo" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none;
                border-bottom: 2px solid #4d3060;
                color: black;">Republican senator</a> from Oklahoma. Mullin is a former mixed martial arts fighter and father of six who grew a family plumbing business.  A strong Trump supporter, he backs tough immigration enforcement and has defended the US Department of Homeland Security and ICE. Known for his fiery style, Mullin has clashed publicly with critics, including during a tense hearing with Sean O'Brien.</p>
</mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>

<mj-spacer height="10px" />
