<mj-section
  background-color="#eff1f4"
  css-class="border-line"
  padding="1px 0.5px 1px 1px"
  border-radius="5px"
>
  <mj-column background-color="#fff" border-radius="5px" padding="0px">
    <mj-spacer height="10px" />
    <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif;" color="#000000">
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 400; margin-top: 2px !important;">
    Addiction Breakthrough?
  </h2>
</mj-text>
<mj-image
  border-radius="10px"
  padding="10px 12px"
  width="600px"
  src="https://www.presidentialsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
  alt="Addiction Breakthrough?"
  href="https://www.presidentialsummary.com/"
/>
<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>What’s happening?</strong> GLP-1 drugs like Ozempic, Wegovy, and Mounjaro, widely used for diabetes and obesity, <a href="https://edition.cnn.com/2026/03/04/health/glp1-addiction-treatment" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none;
                border-bottom: 2px solid #4d3060;
                color: black;">may combat addiction</a> across major substances. A large study of over 600,000 veterans with type 2 diabetes found GLP-1 users faced a 14% lower risk of developing any substance use disorder compared to those on SGLT2 inhibitors (translating to seven fewer cases per 1,000 over three years).</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>How does it work?</strong> GLP-1 drugs mimic the glucagon-like peptide-1 hormone, which helps regulate blood sugar, digestion, and appetite. They react on receptors in both the gut and brain, slowing digestion, increasing insulin release, and reducing hunger signals. Importantly, these medicines also interact with the brain’s reward pathways, particularly areas linked to dopamine and craving. By dampening the brain’s response to rewarding stimuli, they may reduce compulsive behaviors such as overeating, alcohol use, or drug consumption.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>Bigger picture:</strong> Experts caution that the findings remain preliminary. Much of the evidence comes from observational studies rather than controlled clinical trials. Researchers also note that existing data comes largely from older male populations, raising questions about whether the benefits apply broadly.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong><em>Fact:</em></strong><em> About 50Mn people in the US are living with a substance use disorder.</em></p>
</mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
    <mj-spacer height="10px" />
    <mj-section
      background-color="#eff1f4"
